# Update the user manual with the app

Ba ships a public user manual at `public/manual.html` (live: `https://sonatudu.github.io/ba/manual.html`). New users read it to learn screens, buttons, and gestures.

Whenever you add, remove, rename, or change behavior of a user-visible control or feature:

1. Update `public/manual.html` in the same change.
2. Document the **button or control name as shown in the UI** and what it does.
3. Cover every affected screen (Home, Chat, Routine, Daily, Where, To Do, Overview, Memories, Periods, Family, Settings, welcome/login).
4. Add a dated bullet under **Recent updates** (newest first) and set **Last updated**.
5. If you add a new top-level screen, add it to the table of contents and a full section.
6. Do not document secrets (room code digits, setup answer keys).

Skip the manual only for purely internal refactors with no UI or behavior change.
